# The fuzzer's saved crashers are exact byte sequences. Without this, git's
# autocrlf rewrites the newlines in them on checkout -- which changes the input
# and quietly turns every saved case into a different one that no longer
# reproduces the bug it was kept for.
test/corpus/**/*.bin binary

# The same hazard for the seed files, which are not crashers but real MP3s: a
# newline rewritten inside a frame is a frame that decodes to noise, and the
# diff that did it shows nothing.
test/seeds/**/*.mp3 binary
